WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.910
Before their deaths, the following actors
didn't just make their marks as some of Marvel's

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.350
most popular or interesting characters.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.750
They left behind impressive bodies of work,
with Hollywood being all the better for their contributions.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.228
These stars weren't just Marvel favorites,
they built some of Hollywood's most distinguished careers.

00:00:19.034 --> 00:00:22.680
Miguel Ferrer comes from a major show business
family.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.570
His cousin was superstar George Clooney and
his parents were Oscar-winner Jose Ferrer

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.653
and '50s pop star Rosemary Clooney.

00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:35.730
David Lynch fans remember Ferrer as the opinionated
FBI agent Albert Rosenfield on Twin Peaks.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:41.399
Ferrer also co-starred in the 1994 adaptation
of Stephen King's The Stand, playing Randall

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:43.813
Flagg's right-hand man, Lloyd Henreid.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.120
Apart from his dozens of other TV guest star
roles, Ferrer made memorable appearances in

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.556
films including Traffic, Hot Shots: Part Deux,
and RoboCop.

00:00:53.695 --> 00:00:58.530
But observant Marvel Cinematic Universe fans
will remember him for his brief but important

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.072
part in Iron Man 3.

00:01:00.142 --> 00:01:04.976
In the final entry of the trilogy, Ferrer
played Rodriguez, the corrupt, Mandarin-connected

00:01:04.976 --> 00:01:09.909
vice president of the United States who tries
to help assassinate President Matthew Ellis.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:16.670
Sadly, in January 2017, Ferrer died of cancer-related
complications at the age of 61.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:23.575
When stand-up comedy boomed in the 1980s and
early 1990s, tons of clubs popped up in cities,

00:01:23.575 --> 00:01:27.869
cable networks filled out their programming
day with shows like An Evening at the Improv

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:33.101
and The HBO Comedy Half-Hour, and a ton of
joke-tellers became instantly famous.

00:01:33.216 --> 00:01:37.080
Among them was John Pinette, a gifted stand-up
and impressionist.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.710
Pinette dedicated a lot of his act to making
fun of himself.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.820
He toured and taped comedy specials extensively
while also landing acting roles.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.219
After playing a high school coach on Parker
Lewis Can't Lose, he appeared on Seinfeld,

00:01:49.219 --> 00:01:54.950
Dr. Katz: Professional Therapist, and in 2004,
he showed up as Bumpo in the ultra-violent

00:01:54.950 --> 00:02:00.450
film adaptation of the ultra-violent revenge
comic The Punisher, opposite Thomas Jane.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.701
Pinette brought comic relief to the otherwise
dark movie as the easy-going character and

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:07.509
the financial beneficiary of the Punisher's
crusade.

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:12.730
Tragically, in 2014, Pinette was found dead
in a Pittsburgh hotel room, and a medical

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.470
examiner ruled that he'd passed as a result
of natural causes.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.000
Pinette was only 50.

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:23.970
In 1969, Peter Fonda produced and starred
in the hippie and counterculture classic biker

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:28.935
movie Easy Rider, for which he received his
first of two Academy Award nominations.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:34.720
The second came for 1997's Ulee's Gold, in
which Fonda starred as a grieving beekeeper

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:35.910
with a troubled family.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:41.010
In between, Fonda appeared in dozens of well-known
movies, including The Last Movie, The Cannonball

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.890
Run, and Escape from L.A.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:48.935
Fonda's role in Ghost Rider as Mephistopheles
was among the last in a long, legendary career.

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:53.930
"Far out."

00:02:55.349 --> 00:03:01.200
In 2007, actor and avid comic book fan Nick
Cage got his superhero franchise going with

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.010
two Ghost Rider movies.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:08.560
Cage played Johnny Blaze, a bounty hunter
forced into service for the unholy demon played by Fonda.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.360
In 2019, Fonda passed away at age 79 due to
lung cancer.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:19.895
Just before 2010, Irrfan Khan got acting gigs
in popular and acclaimed American and British films.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.400
He played a police detective in the Oscar-nominated
Slumdog Millionaire, and he portrayed the

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.091
adult version of main character Pi Patel,
recalling his survival of a shipwreck, in

00:03:29.091 --> 00:03:31.250
the Oscar-nominated Life of Pi.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:36.260
Khan showed up as dinosaur park owner Simon
Masrani in Jurassic World and he also played

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.316
the villainous Provost in Inferno.

00:03:38.316 --> 00:03:43.310
Fans of Andrew Garflield's Peter Parker will
also recognize Khan from The Amazing Spider-Man,

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:47.501
where he played Oscorp executive and scientist
Dr. Rajit Ratha.

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:51.690
As a prolific television actor, Khan broke
through to the A-list of Indian cinema in

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:57.560
the 2000s and won numerous accolades for his
work in Life in a Metro, Haasil, and Paan

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.734
Singh Tomar, which won him a National Film
Award for Best Actor.

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:07.556
Shockingly, in 2018, Khan announced that he'd
been diagnosed with a neuroendocrine tumor.

00:04:07.556 --> 00:04:13.794
Following a hospitalization in Mumbai for
an infection in 2020, the superstar died at age 53.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:19.151
In 2008, Iron Man became the first Marvel
Cinematic Universe entry.

00:04:19.151 --> 00:04:24.210
But the modern history of movies based on
Marvel Comics characters goes back to 1986,

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.880
with the critically reviled box office flop,
Howard the Duck.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:32.970
Protagonist Howard is involved in everything
sci-fi, including the Cosmos itself, personified

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.668
and voiced by veteran actor Richard Kiley.

00:04:36.799 --> 00:04:38.622
"The cosmos.

00:04:39.498 --> 00:04:42.612
Countless worlds upon worlds."

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:48.380
Kiley was a decorated actor, appearing in
shows like Hawaii Five-O and Columbo and won

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.880
four Emmy Awards and two Tony Awards, including
one for Man of La Mancha.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.470
Kiley died in march 1999 of a blood disorder.

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:57.470
He was 76 years old.

00:04:58.607 --> 00:05:03.690
As one of film and TV's most prolific, intense,
and versatile character actors, it's hard

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:08.413
to say exactly which role is the one for which
Reg E. Cathey is best known.

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:13.880
It might be warden Martin Querns on the harrowing
prison drama Oz, or political organizer Norman

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:19.220
Wilson on The Wire, or barbecue joint proprietor
Freddy Hayes on House of Cards, which won

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.169
Cathey an Emmy Award for Outstanding Guest
Actor in a Drama Series.

00:05:23.253 --> 00:05:26.935
Cathey also played more than one role in multiple
Marvel franchises.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:33.110
In the 2015 Fantastic Four reboot, he portrayed
Dr. Franklin Storm, father of superheroes

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.601
Sue and Johnny Storm.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:39.950
Cathey also starred in Netflix Marvel Cinematic
Universe-adjacent series Luke Cage, in the

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:43.034
role of James Lucas, a pastor and the father
of Luke.

00:05:43.034 --> 00:05:48.801
In February 2018, Cathey died at his New York
City home from lung cancer, according to the New York Times.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.020
Cathey was 59.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:55.260
Dr. Wesley Von Spears appeared briefly in
both Guardians of the Galaxy films.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:06:00.970
He didn't have any lines, but he was memorable
just the same, because Von Spears is a dog.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:05.090
In Guardians of the Galaxy, the pup portrayed
"Holographic Dog," and in Guardians of the

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:09.580
Galaxy Vol. 2 he played the part of "Dog in
the Back of Truck at Dairy Queen."

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:13.800
Landing a role in Hollywood is sometimes about
who you know, and nepotism definitely played

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:18.340
a part in Von Spears' casting since he was
the pet of Guardians writer-director James

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.340
Gunn.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:23.169
The dog's influence on Marvel movies comprises
more than just a couple of cameos.

00:06:23.169 --> 00:06:24.540
Gunn told i09:

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:28.440
"Truthfully, a lot of Groot is based on my
dog Von Spears.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.710
I think there's a sort of puppy-like innocence
to Groot.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:35.389
That if my dog could talk, it would probably
say, 'I am Groot.'"

00:06:35.389 --> 00:06:39.450
Dr. Wesley Von Spears died at age 17 in February
2020.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:44.440
Gunn briefly delayed filming on his next film,
The Suicide Squad, to fly home and be with

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.960
his dog in his final moments.

